I guess you're right. Corporal Nagai. The vehicle is prepped and it is ready to go.

68
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:13,500
I'll take them as close as I can to the Western defense. Remain on high alert.

69
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:18,500
All right. Let's get moving.

70
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:26,500
Well, looky here. It's already started. The vampires aren't pulling any punches.

71
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:32,500
Now, which one of them is the commander?

72
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:51,500
What? You've got to be kidding. He can see me from that far away?

73
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:58,500
Um, Lieutenant Colonel Gurren? You don't seem to be too concerned about this fight.

74
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:08,500
It's not like I'm just slacking off up here, Sayuri. I'm keeping tabs on the vampire commander and enemy troop movements in case the bastards decide to target this outpost as well.

75
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:11,500
Damn. I should have known. Speaking of the devils, watch out.

76
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:25,500
Took you long enough, Mito.

77
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:31,500
Are you saying I'm late? You're the one who called me here on such short notice. So what's with the big hurry?

78
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:34,500
Gurren, sir. We've returned from our mission.

79
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:39,500
It looks like things are going to hell fast. What do you propose we do about it?

80
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:44,500
